# claude-config (Cursor)

This machine runs the claude-config stack. Source of truth: the repo in `~/.claude-tools/config-repo` (or this clone).

## MCP

One gateway: **mcptoon** (`mcptoon serve` in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`). Upstream servers (browsers, serena, figcraft, semgrep, jcodemunch, …) stay behind it — use `mcptoon_manifest`, `mcptoon_inspect`, `mcptoon_call`. Do not expect 20 raw MCP servers in the Cursor MCP list.

## Skills

User skills live in `~/.claude/skills` (base install). Cursor loads them; do not maintain a second copy under `~/.cursor/skills` unless a skill is Cursor-only.

## Project memory

In repos with `.agent/`: read `.agent/handoff.md` then `.agent/memory/MEMORY.md` before changing anything. Write durable facts one-per-file under `.agent/memory/`. User-stated facts and open threads also go to `obsidian-wiki memory profile set|todo add`. For who-calls/what-breaks questions use Serena, codegraph or jCodeMunch through mcptoon before grep loops. Never commit secrets.

Tool roles: exact string or known file = grep/read; "how does X work" = `codegraph_codegraph_explore`; symbols, references, refactors = Serena; callers, impact, dead code = jCodeMunch (`fallow_*` for JS/TS); semantic search = `lumen_semantic_search`; library docs = `context7`; large output = context-mode `ctx_execute`; browser = `lightpanda_*` through the gateway. Gateway form: `mcptoon_call {name: "<server>_<tool>", arguments}`.

## Windows note

If a hook tries to run a bare `.sh` and Windows shows “Select an app…”, re-run `pwsh ./install-cursor.ps1` (wraps Claude `.sh` hooks Cursor also loads). Prefer `.cmd` / `node` / absolute `bash.exe` for any new Cursor hooks.
